  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Nff5edea15944450e857a4f480c3d09de">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/hasAttenuation"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/V_000010_Solid"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/B2_NoduleThatIsAMass">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE B2 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: something that is both a nodule and a mass</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The current definition model declares PulmonaryNodule and PulmonaryMass disjoint. This probe verifies that the class distinction remains reasoner-enforced rather than only a naming convention. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N1ba5e5f46a3c48108ebf3a4e57366997"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group B] expect: unsatisfiable. The current definition model declares PulmonaryNodule and PulmonaryMass disjoint. This probe verifies that the class distinction remains reasoner-enforced rather than only a naming convention.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N1339274bb11e46dc9a613fb272e0d5bd">
    <rdf:first rdf:nodeID="N435a61d1bc3b485dad923602979d8375"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:nodeID="N404ae0a75b25487191a08fc82ea9cbca"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E11_EpiduralCannotBeCrescentic">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E11 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: an epidural hematoma with crescentic collection shape</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The current alpha provisionally models epidural hematoma with a fixed biconvex collection-shape constraint. Collection shape is single-select, so asserting crescentic tests whether the fixed-value mechanism makes the modeled combination inconsistent. This is a mechanism test, not a radiologist-validated clinical rule. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N01d50a9935b24af1aed978204d5268aa"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: unsatisfiable. The current alpha provisionally models epidural hematoma with a fixed biconvex collection-shape constraint. Collection shape is single-select, so asserting crescentic tests whether the fixed-value mechanism makes the modeled combination inconsistent. This is a mechanism test, not a radiologist-validated clinical rule.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N0ebfe5c12c3643ffaf9eb092bfb6f95a">
    <rdf:first rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/FindingClass"/>
    <rdf:rest rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E5_MultiSelectAllowsTwoValues">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E5 [EXPECT CONSISTENT and nothing further - stays where it is, no yellow rows]: a pulmonary nodule with popcorn and punctate calcification</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The counterpart to B1. Calcification is deliberately multi-select, so two patterns co-occurring must remain satisfiable. If this goes red, something has declared the element functional and a lesion can no longer carry two calcification patterns. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N150a3d5ab41d4480b8713ba293f50b52"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: SATISFIABLE. The counterpart to B1. Calcification is deliberately multi-select, so two patterns co-occurring must remain satisfiable. If this goes red, something has declared the element functional and a lesion can no longer carry two calcification patterns.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/A6_CystWithMuralNodule">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE A6 [EXPECT SUBCLASS of an existing class - yellow row in SubClass Of, moves in the tree when the dropdown is set to Inferred]: a cyst with a mural nodule component</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The second conditional-relationship case, and it fires in the opposite direction from the part-solid one. Nothing here asserts a composition value. The chain is: a mural nodule is necessarily componentOf some ComplexCyst, componentOf is functional, so the cyst holding it IS that complex cyst. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N74a0d74088c74ff9b80916ce9edb5553"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group A] expect: subsumed by ComplexRenalCyst. The second conditional-relationship case, and it fires in the opposite direction from the part-solid one. Nothing here asserts a composition value. The chain is: a mural nodule is necessarily componentOf some ComplexCyst, componentOf is functional, so the cyst holding it IS that complex cyst.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="Neccb626a86ee432f976913c6e91681c3">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction"/>
    <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/mayProgressTo"/>
    <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/Empyema"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E2_KidneyContainedInRetroperitoneum">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E2 [EXPECT CONSISTENT and nothing further - stays where it is, no yellow rows]: native kidney Contained_In retroperitoneum relationship</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. Preserves the distinct native Contained_In fact alongside Part_Of. The CDE layer does not rewrite either predicate or use one as a proxy for the other. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N0cda697505dc4b2b8c3c41aef101e707"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: SATISFIABLE. Preserves the distinct native Contained_In fact alongside Part_Of. The CDE layer does not rewrite either predicate or use one as a proxy for the other.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/D1_FindingClassWithNoAnatomicAnchor">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE D1 [EXPECT CONSISTENT and nothing further - stays where it is, no yellow rows]: a finding class with no anatomic anchor</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The requirement that a top-level FindingClass have an anatomic scope is an authoring lint rule, not an OWL axiom. A reasoner therefore should not make this primitive test class inconsistent merely because it lacks a location. This probe keeps the boundary between authoring validation and ontology semantics explicit. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="Neb022baee4f34f1a89c2cfc806665a4b"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group D] expect: SATISFIABLE - expected to stay white. The requirement that a top-level FindingClass have an anatomic scope is an authoring lint rule, not an OWL axiom. A reasoner therefore should not make this primitive test class inconsistent merely because it lacks a location. This probe keeps the boundary between authoring validation and ontology semantics explicit.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E6_SingleSelectOnAcuity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E6 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: a rib fracture that is both acute and healed</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. Acuity is single-select. Disjoint values alone would not catch this, because two different fillers are possible; it is caught because the property is declared functional. Removing either the disjointness or the functional declaration turns this white. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N9c3c323ccd3a420dab53f58aac2a8fb5"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: unsatisfiable. Acuity is single-select. Disjoint values alone would not catch this, because two different fillers are possible; it is caught because the property is declared functional. Removing either the disjointness or the functional declaration turns this white.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
