  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/A3_PartSolidByAttenuation">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE A3 [EXPECT EQUIVALENT to an existing class - yellow row in Equivalent To, does NOT move in the tree]: a pulmonary nodule whose attenuation is part-solid</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The condition-versus-subtype case. The subtype is defined, so nobody authors it twice and the component requirement attaches to it automatically. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Ndcb93425c1ef41268bdda7155181970e"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group A] expect: subsumed by PartSolidPulmonaryNodule. The condition-versus-subtype case. The subtype is defined, so nobody authors it twice and the component requirement attaches to it automatically.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/B3_RibFractureWithChronicAcuity">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE B3 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: a rib fracture reported as chronic</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. RibFracture narrows Acuity to acute, healing, healed, or indeterminate age. Chronic remains a value of the reusable Acuity DataElement but is excluded at this point of use with an allValuesFrom restriction. This probe verifies that the class-specific narrowing is reasoner-enforced. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Na0735a5df6254e71b5fe4541338e719d"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group B] expect: unsatisfiable. RibFracture narrows Acuity to acute, healing, healed, or indeterminate age. Chronic remains a value of the reusable Acuity DataElement but is excluded at this point of use with an allValuesFrom restriction. This probe verifies that the class-specific narrowing is reasoner-enforced.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/radcde-probes">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <owl:imports rdf:resource="https://radelement.org/ng/radcde-alpha"/>
    <dcterms:title>RadElement next-gen alpha: probes</dcterms:title>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test cases. Run a reasoner over this module. Group A probes should classify under something informative. Group B probes should go red. A Group B probe that stays white means the constraint it tests is not being enforced.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E7_AtelectasisAxesAreIndependent">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E7 [EXPECT CONSISTENT and nothing further - stays where it is, no yellow rows]: compressive atelectasis with a rounded morphology</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The restructure that replaced five atelectasis subtypes with two elements rests on the axes being independent: a rounded atelectasis is characteristically compressive. If this ever goes red the two have been made to partition one another, and the subtype question reopens. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N9863ee8fbc334df49fc4e257edda3f99"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: SATISFIABLE. The restructure that replaced five atelectasis subtypes with two elements rests on the axes being independent: a rounded atelectasis is characteristically compressive. If this ever goes red the two have been made to partition one another, and the subtype question reopens.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E1_KidneyPartOfUrinaryTract">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E1 [EXPECT CONSISTENT and nothing further - stays where it is, no yellow rows]: native kidney Part_Of urinary tract relationship</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. Preserves the exact native Part_Of predicate. This probe does not authorize any application traversal or substitution with another RadLex property. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N4d2ab5abdfbc4714831aebbc61bb4c3c"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: SATISFIABLE. Preserves the exact native Part_Of predicate. This probe does not authorize any application traversal or substitution with another RadLex property.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
