  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/E12_SubduralCannotBeBiconvex">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE E12 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: a subdural hematoma with biconvex collection shape</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The current alpha provisionally models subdural hematoma with a fixed crescentic collection-shape constraint. Collection shape is single-select, so asserting biconvex tests whether the fixed-value mechanism makes the modeled combination inconsistent. This is a mechanism test, not a radiologist-validated clinical rule. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="Nf3722b4f24804cd98700093e6dff561d"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group E] expect: unsatisfiable. The current alpha provisionally models subdural hematoma with a fixed crescentic collection-shape constraint. Collection shape is single-select, so asserting biconvex tests whether the fixed-value mechanism makes the modeled combination inconsistent. This is a mechanism test, not a radiologist-validated clinical rule.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
