  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://radelement.org/ng/probe/B6_SimpleCystWithMuralNodule">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <rdfs:label>PROBE B6 [EXPECT INCONSISTENT - turns red under owl:Nothing]: a simple cyst with a mural nodule</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>Deliberate test case, not part of the vocabulary. The conditional actually bites. SimpleCyst fixes composition to cystic; the mural nodule forces the same cyst to be a ComplexCyst, whose composition is mixed cystic and solid. hasComposition is functional (D-02) and the two values are disjoint, so the contradiction surfaces. Note this needed three separate decisions to work: functional componentOf, functional hasComposition, and disjoint values. Remove any one and this probe goes white. If this probe does not do what its label says, a constraint has been lost or added. Only inconsistency shows as colour, so a probe expecting EQUIVALENT or SUBCLASS fails silently: check the Description panel, where the reasoner's conclusions appear as yellow rows, rather than looking for a colour in the tree.</rdfs:comment>
    <owl:equivalentClass rdf:nodeID="N1b9561656a03478d8cc4bbe4ec910a2a"/>
    <cde:designNote>[Group B] expect: unsatisfiable. The conditional actually bites. SimpleCyst fixes composition to cystic; the mural nodule forces the same cyst to be a ComplexCyst, whose composition is mixed cystic and solid. hasComposition is functional (D-02) and the two values are disjoint, so the contradiction surfaces. Note this needed three separate decisions to work: functional componentOf, functional hasComposition, and disjoint values. Remove any one and this probe goes white.</cde:designNote>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N9863ee8fbc334df49fc4e257edda3f99">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <owl:intersectionOf rdf:nodeID="Nc58ccc089e424478a5977c0a675b29b2"/>
